@startuml resolve
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Resolve — 3 phases: attack → move → fog approach

start

:Take planning snap — turn N is open;

:**Turn-open legal king-checks** — ""beginScTurn"" — fog-visible, implicit,\nwhite then black — ""applyPendingCCShots"".\nResolved **before** players choose intent. A unit that\nbreaks contact later this turn already paid a **parting shot**;

if (the two kings are adjacent?) then (yes)
  :**King duel** — a king is a legal checker of the enemy king.\nThe collector loops **both** king colours independently, so\ncontact is always **mutual**. Damage is **per checker**: every\nunit checking a king costs it 1 HP, so N checkers = N HP.\nKings leap — ""leapsPiece"" — never the blocker / collision\nbranch: adjacency always chips, nothing is captured, the\nplacement is untouched;
  note right
    Same-pass retaliation does not require
    positive remaining HP on the shooter.
    Per-checker damage therefore preserves
    mutual draws rather than introducing
    a White-first resolution advantage.
  end note
else (no)
  :Only checkers with clear geometry to the king chip;
endif

if (either king at 0 HP after turn-open checks?) then (yes)
  :Phase O — no intent / B / C / F;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Players queue intent (specials + classical);

:End / timeout — ""endScTurn"" — live passes\n""skipTurnStartChecks"" when checks already applied;

:require phase P, queue shape, then both sides'\nprospective C dependencies before optional checks\nor an early terminal return;
note right
  Native preflight rejects impossible C shapes
  before turn-open damage can settle the queue.
  Skip-turn-start mode bypasses checks only,
  rather than bypassing dependency validation.
end note
:when start checks are not skipped, apply End's\nexisting check branch; a terminal return occurs\nonly after that mandatory preflight;

:Apply rank **B** specials — white then black\n— spawn / mine / warp / siege;\n**Presentation:** gas absorb VFX — canister drops\nfrom the top of the actor square — left / mid / right —\ninto the unit; green special-used aura eases in;

note right
  Unheld gas steps, drops and jumps do not
  attack their destination before arrival.
  Hostile mines destroy both participants,
  while allied mines remain armed underfoot.
end note
:record actual B identities: fresh deployment,\nreal transfer, destruction and surviving promotion;
note right
  A deployment crush and newborn mine death
  remain separate native lifecycle effects.
  Equal square and type cannot identify
  the transferred Marine-double carrier.
end note
:retain B/F arrival cues and fields:\nqj / qjm / qjd; armm / armd;\nvictim / unit / mineColor / chaseFrom / collider;
note right
  Visible mines remain script avoidance targets.
  Native contact still owns actual survival.
end note

:Rank **C** — classical for both sides against\nthe same start board — ""resolveTurn"";
:preserve native B normalization and held arrivals;\ncheck actual last-rank promotion at End;\nissue matched-double facts only on a fresh native input;
:capture plan scalars; consume and delete native binding;\nguard both live C actors before recorder,\nvisibility callback, query or classical effect;
note right
  Both live same-side actors require physical
  geometry or a matched native Marine double.
  Missing or foreign actors retain their
  dropped-action behavior without geometry errors.
end note

note right
  A B relocate that departs
  relinquishes its origin for all
  subsequent landings this turn.
  Ordered resolve retires the mover
  before recording any arrival.
end note

:Phase 1 **attack** — direct attacks on targets visible\nfrom the start board — attack → death → occupy;

note right
  Mine clearing requires a visible reachable
  target that the mover attacks on arrival.
  Marine forward movement remains a walk,
  so contact destroys it instead of supplying
  a free forward capture or promotion.
end note
:mine walk: fogged or intermediate hostile contact\nchases to the actual landing; Marine doubles walk\nthe intermediate square, Hoverbikes and CCs leap;
note right
  Extra Step extends the same contact walk
  rather than creating unrelated arrivals.
  CC contact clears in every mode, whereas
  allied mines never inflict friendly damage.
end note

note right
  Forward Marine movement truncates before
  any occupant, including an enemy CC.
  Diagonal captures remain separate, and
  a head-on race onto empty ground can still
  destroy both movers during the move phase.
end note

if (attack hits a piece?) then (yes)
  :Death — victim removed;
  if (attacker survives?) then (yes)
    :**Occupy** victim's square;
  else (no)
    :Attacker dies first — square stays empty, no occupy;
  endif
elseif (attack hits a visible hostile **mine**?) then (yes)
  :""mineBlast"" in ""attacks"" — the **mine** dies (no victim);\nattacker **occupies** the tile — a sieged tank clears it\nwithout relocating (""firesInPlace"");
else (no)
  if (sieged rook shells empty cross?\nempty ""to"" on file/rank, clear ray, visible) then (yes)
    :""shelling"" in ""attacks"" — victimless HE at ""to"";\nno death, no occupy, tank holds (""firesInPlace"");\nclear ray only — mid-ray enemy captured upstream,\nally/king contact holds fire, fogged stays quiet;
  else (no)
    :No direct hit — quiet intent defers to phase 2;
  endif
endif

:Phase 2 **move** — survivors relocate; collisions\nresolved against the post-attack board; a target\n**still fogged at contact** → move collision\n— capture/occupy, no attack cue (never a\n**marine front step** — that blocks + truncates);\n**timed race** (""move-timing.puml""): movers meet where\none reaches a square the other holds — parked, same\ntick, or head-on → **both die** there, no attack cue;\ncolour and plan order never decide it;

:Phase 3 **fog approach** — path-reveal shots slide\n""pathRevealFrom"" → discovery square → attack;\n**King HP mid-resolve** only here: fog intent finds a\nhidden king on the path — ""pathReveal"" ccShot.\nVisible kings already paid at turn open — no second chip.\n**fizzle unless** the attacker still occupies\n""pathRevealFrom"" — died in phases 1–2 / square\nre-occupied by a phase-2 mover / sieged — rooks\nnever relocate — and ""to"" holds the exact\nin-the-way victim;

note right
  Fog approaches select unit targets, not mines,
  so traversal cannot clear hostile contact.
  The applied capture or CC damage persists
  despite the mover's later destruction
  during native mine-contact processing.
end note
:retain approach fields and cues:\npathRevealFrom / pathRevealSteps / stopAt;\npathRevealMineTriggers: prmm / prm / prv\nreplayed from the afterMove mine snapshot;
note right
  CC: no fog-approach slide.
  Allied mines: inert contact.
end note

:Apply rank **F** specials — white then black\n— post-move siege / late drops;\n**Presentation:** same gas absorb drop + aura as B;

if (either king at 0 HP after all ranks?) then (yes)
  :Next snap phase **O** — terminal and **absorbing**;
  :""endScTurn"" throws on a non-P snapshot;
  :""scOutcome"" from ccLives — 0/0 draw, else win;
else (no)
  :Next snap phase **P** — play continues;
endif

note right
  Promotion requires a Marine that survived
  movement and every actual mine contact.
  A last-rank diagonal mine capture clears
  the target before occupancy, so survival
  can still permit the queued transformation.
end note
:promotion playback: one MOVE_SQUARE_MS walk\noff the edge, then deploy the selected unit;\nno surviving Marine means no promotion animation;

stop

' Approach gates remain in resolve-turn-activity: siege, destinationsWritten,
' live actor at pathRevealFrom and exact victim type/color; only fired approaches are returned.
' Attack application leaves mine spending to the native phase-3 walk-contact site.
' Output groups remain attacks; moves/mineTriggers/moveCollisions;
' pathRevealAttacks/pathRevealMineTriggers, with afterMove and afterAll snapshots.
' A fog-discovered CC shot stops before the CC and retains its damage;
' turn-open checks remain visibility-gated, and no direct C aim occupies a CC.
' CC duel preserves per-checker damage, same-pass retaliation at zero HP,
' placement, equal-HP draw and added deployment checkers; departure cannot undo a parting shot.
' Terminal checks skip B/C/F; terminal simultaneous C skips F only.
' Outcome derives from CC lives and the existing turn cap (45), not a persisted winner field.
' Existing phase O and dead-CC parsing rules remain unchanged; no SCFEN grammar amendment.
@enduml
